 "findings": [
  {
   "heading": "\"Adorning\" the tabyl",
   "segment_index": "S11.P1",
   "kind": "code_mismatch",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:173-173",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.fr.qmd:164-164",
   "proposition": "The French table row states the arguments of `adorn_totals()` are `où =` and `nom =`, taking the values \" ligne \", \" colonne \" or \" les deux \"; the actual arguments are `where =` and `name =` with values \"row\", \"col\" and \"both\", as used in the chunk at chapters/tables_descriptive.fr.qmd:189-195.",
   "reader_consequence": "A French reader writing `adorn_totals(où = \"ligne\")` gets an \"unused argument\" error and cannot reproduce the total row shown in the examples.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "\"Adorning\" the tabyl",
   "segment_index": "S11.P1",
   "kind": "code_mismatch",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:174-174",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.fr.qmd:166-166",
   "proposition": "The French table row names the `adorn_percentages()` argument `denominateur =` with values \" ligne \", \" colonne \", \" tout \"; the real argument is `denominator =` with values \"row\", \"col\", \"all\", as used in the chunk at chapters/tables_descriptive.fr.qmd:189-195.",
   "reader_consequence": "A French reader copying `adorn_percentages(denominateur = \"ligne\")` gets an error instead of row proportions.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "\"Adorning\" the tabyl",
   "segment_index": "S11.P1",
   "kind": "code_mismatch",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:177-177",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.fr.qmd:172-172",
   "proposition": "The French table row states `position =` takes the values \"arrière\" and \"avant\"; `adorn_ns()` accepts only \"rear\" and \"front\", and the chunk at chapters/tables_descriptive.fr.qmd:199-209 uses `position = \"front\"`.",
   "reader_consequence": "A French reader passing `position = \"avant\"` gets an error and cannot place counts before percents.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Adjustments",
   "segment_index": "S34.P1",
   "kind": "code_mismatch",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:864-864",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.fr.qmd:833-833",
   "proposition": "The English says the statistics go \"within curly brackets\" in the `statistic =` string; the French says \"entre crochets\" (square brackets), while the chunk beside it at chapters/tables_descriptive.fr.qmd:838-843 uses `\"{mean}\"` with curly braces.",
   "reader_consequence": "A French reader writes `statistic = age_years ~ \"[mean]\"`, which gtsummary prints literally instead of substituting the mean.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Adjustments",
   "segment_index": "S34.P3",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:893-894",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.fr.qmd:862-863",
   "proposition": "The French states the default value of `missing_text =` is \"Inconnu\"; the gtsummary default is the English string \"Unknown\".",
   "reader_consequence": "A French reader expects the table to print \"Inconnu\" without setting `missing_text =`, and cannot predict or match the label that actually appears.",
   "confidence": "high"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Summary table",
   "segment_index": "S33.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:845-845",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.fr.qmd:815-815",
   "proposition": "The French states that missing values are converted to \"Inconnu\" by the default `tbl_summary()`; the table produced by the chunk at chapters/tables_descriptive.fr.qmd:817-821 shows \"Unknown\".",
   "reader_consequence": "A French reader looking for an \"Inconnu\" row in the printed output does not find one and may think the missing-value handling failed.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Multi-line stats for continuous variables",
   "segment_index": "S35.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:926-926",
