  },
  {
   "heading": "Show all levels",
   "segment_index": "S19.P1",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.qmd:348-348",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_descriptive.fr.qmd:337-337",
   "proposition": "The English motivates `.drop = FALSE` by the case of creating figures (plots) for multiple sub-groups and repeating the same figure for routine reports; the French says \"chiffres\" (numbers/digits), so it claims the technique is about producing numbers rather than plots.",
   "reader_consequence": "A French reader misses that the argument exists to keep plot axes and legends constant across sub-groups and repeated reports, which is the reason to use it.",
